            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0644" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.73/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-07T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 8—9:47
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Referring to the Department’s number 2, February 4, 7 p.m.<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d261-f1"/> Western Telegraph Company today presented to the
                    Uruguayan Minister of Industry a communication embodying resolution of London
                    company, also handing me copy as arranged. I am to be informed of the
                    Government’s reply and shall telegraph answer at once; meanwhile, I am in close
                    touch with the manager of the All America Cables.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
